      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a foundational approach for your guide, focusing on clear, systematic examples for high schoolers. Begin by defining \"systemic racism\" as the way institutional and policy bias, rather than individual prejudice, perpetuates inequality in the **lending and real estate market**\n\nFor the **banking side,** discuss **redlining,** where discriminatory government and private bank policies systematically denied the best credit and insurance to specific, often minority, neighborhoods, limiting wealth-building for those residents.\n\nIn **housing,** connect this to **subprime and discriminatory real estate practices,** which have forced the concentration of poverty and under-resourced public services in certain areas, making systemic injustice a clear, *unseen process",
      "source": "target",
